    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346-a1">

                <pb facs="0742" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 7, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my note of the 7th of
                    December last, I have the honor to state to you that, I have been informed by
                    the secretary of state for the colonies, that the governor of the Cape of Good
                    Hope has recognized Mr. Hoets, Mr. Eager, and Mr. Cato, respectively, as
                    consular agents for the United States at Simon’s Bay, Mossel Bay, and Port
                    Natal, but that he has abstained from recognizing Mr. J. C. Hess, who has lately
                    assigned his estate to his creditors, as United States consular agent at Port
                    Elizabeth.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to return herewith the certificates of these gentlemen’s
                    appointment, which were enclosed in your letter of the 4th of December.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
